---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Services" description="AI adoption for engineering teams, one-off AI integration projects, and delivery and engineering leadership.">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Services</h1>
    <p>I take on a small number of engagements at a time and do the work myself. No account managers, no hand-offs.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="services">
    <section class="service">
      <h2>AI adoption for <strong>engineering teams</strong></h2>
      <p>Getting a whole team to ship with coding agents, safely. I work alongside your engineers rather than handing over a slide deck.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Full-day mobbing sessions on real work</li>
        <li>Spec-driven development, agent harnesses and deterministic guardrails</li>
        <li>Automated approvals, sign-offs and DORA reporting, so governance stops being the bottleneck</li>
      </ul>
      <p><em>Seven teams at a major bank reached roughly 90% AI-generated code this way.</em></p>
    </section>
    <section class="service">
      <h2>AI integration <strong>projects</strong></h2>
      <p>A fixed-scope project to put AI to work on one real problem in your business, built to run in production rather than just demo.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Assistants over your own data, driven by tool calls</li>
        <li>Support and back-office automation with a human approving what goes out</li>
        <li>Evaluation, cost controls and monitoring included</li>
      </ul>
      <p><em>Recent builds include a natural-language pricing assistant and a human-in-the-loop customer service system. I also build in Elixir and Phoenix when that's the right tool.</em></p>
    </section>
    <section class="service">
      <h2>Delivery &amp; <strong>leadership</strong></h2>
      <p>For organizations that need to ship more often, scale a team, or put numbers on how delivery is going.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Continuous delivery, trunk-based development and pipelines</li>
        <li>DORA metrics that managers and VPs actually use</li>
        <li>Scaling teams and building the management layer under them</li>
        <li>Interim or fractional engineering leadership</li>
      </ul>
      <p><em>Five-fold deployment frequency on a real-time payments program; 18 teams moved to modern delivery practices.</em></p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top:3rem"><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a></p>
</Base>
